  "result": "Excellent! All **205 tests pass** (20 new voucher tests added).\n\nHere's what I implemented:\n\n**Updated: `src/errors.js`**\n- Added VOUCHER_EXISTS: \"An invoice can only have one voucher.\"\n\n**Updated: `src/invoices.js`**\n- Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function that:\n  - Validates status is 'draft' (returns NOT_DRAFT error)\n  - Prevents applying multiple vouchers (returns VOUCHER_EXISTS error)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (returns AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n  - Sets invoice.voucher = { code, amount }\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to:\n  - Include voucher field in calculation (0 if no voucher applied)\n  - Calculate: `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n  - Clamp total at 0 minimum\n  - Return voucher value in result\n- Updated `addLine()`, `removeLine()`, and `issueInvoice()` to preserve voucher\n\n**Updated: `src/payments.js`**\n- Updated `recordPayment()` to preserve voucher property\n\n**Updated: `test/invoices.test.js`**\n- Fixed 5 existing invoiceTotals tests to expect voucher: 0 in results\n\n**New Tests: `test/vouchers.test.js`** (20 test cases)\n- Adding voucher to draft invoice\n- Rejecting non-draft invoices\n- Preventing multiple vouchers per invoice\n- Validating amount (positive, integer, non-zero)\n- invoiceTotals calculation with vouchers\n- Voucher subtraction from total after VAT\n- Total clamping with large vouchers\n- Voucher preservation through all operations (addLine, removeLine, issueInvoice, recordPayment)\n- Voucher code preservation\n- Immutability verification\n\nThe voucher feature correctly applies a fixed discount after VAT calculation, respecting the house rule of clamping amounts at 0 minimum.",
